stateDiagram-v2
    state "ACTIVE" as active
    state "RETIRED" as retired

    [*] --> active: create anonymous preference
    active --> retired: Base reset or committed Visa sign-out / locked setting transaction

    note right of active
      OrgPreferenceStatus uses ACTIVE=2 and RETIRED=1.
      A valid anonymous JWT identifies the active row.
      Reset and Visa sign-out create a replacement in
      the same setting transaction that retires this row.
      Visa sign-in applies only explicit Operator display
      values; region, consent, Web Push, and binding
      are not imported from the account.
      Visa sign-out copies stored display children
      including region from the old row's database state.
    end note

    note right of retired
      A retired row cannot be reactivated. Its last-issued
      expiry remains the retention anchor. The local
      schema cutover migration is authored but unapproved
      and has not been applied.
    end note
